SlopSync

"SlopSync" names a specific protocol: the one defined in spec/SPEC.md and the
registry it points to. The code (MIT) and the spec text (CC-BY 4.0) are
freely reusable — copy them, adapt them, ship them.

The name is reserved for implementations that actually speak the protocol.
Please don't call something "SlopSync" (or something confusingly close to
it) if it doesn't conform to spec/SPEC.md — call it "SlopSync-inspired" or
name it something else. This keeps the name meaning one thing to anyone who
hears it.

That's it. No trademark filing, no enforcement office — just a request, so
the name stays useful.
